# Inputs from Kotlin Temper's BuildTreeTest (astbuild), named by test
# function, with the tree our grammar step builds, in the form of
# print::write_ast. Tests that start from a production other than Root say
# so; here they're built from Root like any module. compat/check_ast.py
# checks these inputs against Kotlin Temper.
=== annotatedFn
@(A..T) fn f(a) {}
--- ast
(Call @ (Call #desugarOperation .. A T) (Call fn \word ^f a (Fun (Block))))

=== simpleValue
123
--- ast
123

=== trailingSemi
123; 456;
--- ast
(Block 123 456 #void)

=== trailingSemiBlock
do { 123 }
do { 456 };
do { 789 };
--- ast
(Block
  (Call do (Fun (Block 123)))
  (Call do (Fun (Block 456)))
  (Call do (Fun (Block 789)))
  #void)

